> The result of dist() is a vector that represents the portion below the
> diagonal of the (symmetric) distance matrix
>
>    0
>    *  0
>    *  *  0
>    *  *  *  0
>    ...
>
> where the *'s are the values in the vector. The blanks are filled in
> from top to bottom, then left to right. In your case, the matrix would
> be (lower triangular part only)
>
>   0
>   1   0
>   1  0.5  0
>   0   1   1   0
