Here is my example:

plot(x=invitro$x,y=invitro$y,type="l",lty=1,
xlim=c(0,24),ylim=c(0,100),xlab="Time (h)",ylab=" percent dissolved (%)" )
lines(x=invitro1$x,y=invitro2$y,type="l",lty=2 )
legend(x=15, y=40, legend=c("1","2"),lty = c(1,2))
export.graph(Name = "GSD2",ExportType = "WMF",
        FileName = paste(reportDir,"figures\\invitro.observed.WMF",sep=""))

After you use "plot", the graph is created with some name assigned to it. On
my version, it is "CSD2". Then it can be saved as .WMF file and imported to
Word
Leonid

