We have tried the wmf route many times and have consistently found
the graphics to be corrupted if you touch them in Word in any
way.  Postscript, even using the postscript driver in Windows S+,
is much more faithful in my view.  And you can edit postscript
using nice free tools: ghostscript and Mayura Draw.  (First
convert .ps to Adobe Illustrator .ai format with ghostscript,
then edit with Mayura and save as .ps).  The problem is that
this won't work for Powerpoint for screen viewing.  But I'm
abandoning Powerpoint anyway because of a number of shortcomings.
