Message-ID: <Pine.SOL.4.21.0008121137540.18522-100000@pons.uio.no>

I also prefer using UNIX cut prior to scan when reading from 
fixed format files. But I've also had success in using, for 
instance,

scan("C:/temp/testfile.dat", what=list(NULL, 0), width = c(2,3),
flush=T)[[2]]

which skips the first two columns and then read the next three
as a single numeric data vector and finally skips the rest of 
the columns.
The 0 in the what argument can, of course, be replaced by "" 
to read character data.
This has worked fine for me even on pretty big data sets.

