Erin Hodgess <hodgess at uhddx01.dt.uh.edu> wrote -

> acf(is.na(x))

I think Erin meant

acf(x[!is.na(x)])

However the omission of some points will have the result
that the lags determined by acf() will sometimes be wrong,
i.e. the real lag will be greater than the assumed lag.

