Carlos,

> Whenever I start Splus5.1/Linux on my system (Redhat 6.1 on Intel) it
> creates the lock file /tmp/.elmd.6144 and refuses to start, I then have to
> login as root and remove the lock file, at which point Splus will start
> normally.

I have exactly this configuration and am using Splus without problems.  I have 
edited /etc/rc.d/rc.local to add the following lines:

echo "Starting S-PLUS licence server (elmd)"
/usr/local/bin/Splus5 LICENSE server start

However, it looks as if your licence server is starting: it's the licence 
server (elmd) that creates /tmp/.elmd.6144, which contains elmd's PID; this is 
normal behaviour.  But maybe elmd is not terminating normally, and therefore 
isn't cleaning up the lock file itself.

Andrew Runnalls

