Date: Wed, 23 Aug 2000 09:37:03 +0200
Subject: Re: [S] Built-in function for higher moments?
In-Reply-To: <Pine.GSO.4.05.10008220835181.17935-100000@six.reed.edu>
References: <200008221127.GAA21018@wubios.wustl.edu> <Pine.GSO.4.05.10008220835181.17935-100000@six.reed.edu>
Message-ID: <200008230741.CAA22599@wubios.wustl.edu>

I'm happy you found the error in the function - it's the same as in the 
function 
of  Michael Camilleri - we both used the unbiased estimate of the 
variance. So the usual estimate (ML) would be:

skewness <- function(x)
        mean((x - mean(x))^3) / var(x, unbiased=F)^(3/2)

kurtosis <- function(x)
        mean((x - mean(x))^4) / var(x, unbiased=F)^2 - 3

The same applies on the functions of Camilleri.
Meinhard P.
