Subject: Re: [S] request for function to calculate Cronbach alpha reliabilitycoefficient
References: <4FE744BC8170D011B15A00805FEA91B90320DFF8@exchww03.mednet.ucla.edu>
Message-ID: <39A3D562.30847DB4@imap.pitt.edu>

Sure.  Let S be the covariance matrix of the individual measurements

Then

alpha.cronbach<-
function(S)
{
 d <- dim(S)[1]
 (d/(d - 1)) * (1 - sum(diag(S))/sum(S))
}

This function is not bullet-proof against invalid arguments for S (S a
scalar for example).

